    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Concept Overview</h2>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Class Definition</strong>: Creating a blueprint (`class Player:`).</li>
            <li><strong>Attributes</strong>: Storing data (`self.health`, `self.name`).</li>
            <li><strong>Constructor</strong>: Initializing state (`__init__`).</li>
            <li><strong>Methods</strong>: Defining behavior (`take_damage`, `heal`).</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Common Misconceptions</h2>
        <div class="info-content">
            <p><strong>1. Forgetting `self`</strong></p>
            <p>Students often write `health = 100` instead of `self.health = 100`. Explain that `self` attaches the variable to the <em>specific object</em>, whereas a plain variable dies when the function ends.</p>
            
            <p><strong>2. Indentation Errors</strong></p>
            <p>Ensure methods are indented <em>inside</em> the class. If `def __init__` is flush with `class Player`, it won't work.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Solution Code</h2>
        <div class="code-block" style="background: #1e1e1e; color: #d4d4d4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto;">
            <pre><code>class Player:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name
        self.health = 100
        self.max_health = 100
        self.armour = 2
        self.accuracy = 85
        self.inventory = None  # technically Inventory() in later levels
        self.logbook = None

    def get_status(self):
        return f"{self.name}: {self.health}/{self.max_health} HP"

    def take_damage(self, amount):
        # Prevent negative health
        self.health -= amount
        if self.health < 0:
            self.health = 0
            
        # OR use max()
        # self.health = max(0, self.health - amount)

    def heal(self, amount):
        # Prevent overheal
        self.health += amount
        if self.health > self.max_health:
            self.health = self.max_health
            
        # OR use min()
        # self.health = min(self.max_health, self.health + amount)</code></pre>
        </div>
